        "title": "5. Missing error-handling tests",
        "content": "\nNone of the following failure paths are tested anywhere (most can't be yet since the code doesn't exist, but they need to be specified now):\n\n| Missing case | Where it should live |\n|---|---|\n| `main.py::run_status` for a nonexistent `run_id` → currently unconditionally 501; once implemented, must 404 | `engine/tests/test_main.py` |\n| `execute_run` failure mid-pipeline → must write `status=\"failed\"` + `error` and not leave a run stuck in an intermediate status | `engine/tests/test_main.py` |\n| `db.py::update_run_status` called with an invalid `RunStatus` transition (e.g. `complete → matching`) | `engine/tests/test_db.py` |\n| `requireReviewer()` when Clerk session exists but `currentUser()` returns null (edge case between auth() and currentUser() consistency) | `web/lib/server/auth.test.ts` |\n| Zod schema failures on route handlers — **can't be tested yet, no route handlers exist** (Phase 4 item 12+) | flag as not-yet-buildable |\n| `SalesforceConnector`/`WarehouseConnector` — no test for auth failure, rate limiting, empty result set, or partial-page failures mid-stream | `engine/tests/connectors/` (Phase 5) |\n| `SyntheticConnector.extract` on a missing/corrupt `data_dir` | `engine/tests/connectors/test_synthetic.py` |\n\n```python\n",
        "level": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "engine/tests/connectors/test_synthetic.py",
