      {
        "title": "6. Integration test gaps",
        "content": "\nNone of these exist and can't be written meaningfully until the corresponding phase lands, but the seams are worth naming now so they aren't forgotten:\n\n1. **Web ↔ Engine HTTP contract** — `POST {ENGINE_URL}/runs` → `GET /runs/:id/status` round trip. No web-side typed client exists yet (`lib/server/engine.ts` is listed in the architecture but not yet created).\n2. **Table-ownership enforcement** — no automated check that the engine never writes `sources`/`rulesets`, or that web never writes `entities`/`matches`/`conflicts`. This is exactly the kind of invariant that should be a test (e.g., a DB-permission test using a Postgres role with `REVOKE` on those tables for each writer), not just a comment in AGENTS.md.\n3. **Zod ↔ Pydantic contract drift** — no test asserts the two schemas actually agree (e.g., generate example payloads from Pydantic, validate against Zod in a golden-file test, or vice versa). This is explicitly called out in AGENTS.md as something that must never drift.\n4. **Full pipeline run against `eval/generate.py` output** — `extract → normalize → match → detect → resolve` end-to-end, once each stage exists — currently impossible since every stage raises `NotImplementedError`.\n5. **Auth middleware (`proxy.ts`) route coverage** — no test confirms `/api/runs/*` and other non-public routes actually 401/redirect when unauthenticated, versus `/`, `/sign-in`, `/sign-up` staying public.\n\n```ts\n// web/proxy.test.ts (needs a Clerk test harness — @clerk/testing)\nit(\"blocks unauthenticated access to a console route\", async () => {\n  const res = await fetch(\"/runs\", { redirect: \"manual\" });\n  expect([302, 307, 401]).toContain(res.status);\n});\nit(\"allows unauthenticated access to the landing page\", async () => {\n  const res = await fetch(\"/\");\n  expect(res.status).toBe(200);\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n",
        "level": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "Priority order",
        "content": "1. Stand up test infra (`pytest` config in `engine/`, add `vitest` + `@testing-library/react` to `web/` — **ask before installing**, per AGENTS.md's small-dependency-surface rule).\n2. Write real tests for the ~6 already-implemented functions/components (§2–3 above) — zero excuse, they're pure and small.\n3. Land the `xfail` skeletons for Phase 2/3 pipeline + agent functions now, alongside `eval/generate.py`, so implementation is TDD against the documented contract (fold_name, classify, should_auto_apply boundaries, validate's non-negotiable rejection behavior).\n4. Defer connector and full-integration tests until Phase 5/6 per the build order — but keep the seam list in §6 so it isn't rediscovered from scratch later.",
        "level": 3
      }
    ],
